  "_comment": [
    "SHA-256 of values that must never appear in the tracked tree, normalised",
    "by tests/test_no_personal_data.py (casefold, every non-word run collapsed",
    "to one space). Never add a value in clear text here.",
    "This list is a tripwire, not a secret store: a short, low-entropy value",
    "such as a town or a postcode is recoverable from a gazetteer by anyone",
    "who wants to, and the names it covers are in this repository's history",
    "anyway. What it buys is that the value is not readable, greppable or",
    "indexable at the tip, and that it cannot come back unnoticed.",
    "'tokens' is how many normalised tokens the value has; the scanner reads",
    "the largest one to know how wide a window it must hash."
  ],
